EXPERT_ADVISOR_BOT — Installation & Deployment Guide
Purpose: This document is only for installing, configuring, testing and starting EXPERT_ADVISOR_BOT on a Windows PC or an AWS Windows EC2 VPS. The project overview and code architecture belong in README.md.

Live-trading warning: The supplied main.py connects to MetaTrader 5 and runs the Scalping, Intraday, Swing and News pipelines. Its execution path can submit real orders when the terminal and account permit Python trading. There is no verified paper-trading/dry-run switch in the supplied main.py. Complete the initial setup on a DEMO account only. Do not treat installation success as proof of strategy profitability or safety.

1. Installation target and recommended versions
The supplied project is a Windows-oriented Python application that communicates with the locally installed MetaTrader 5 desktop terminal through the MetaTrader5 Python package.
Component	Recommended selection	Notes
Operating system — local	Windows 10/11, 64-bit	Use an x86-64 Windows installation.
Operating system — VPS	Windows Server 2022 Base, x86-64	Use the Windows EC2 AMI, not Ubuntu/Linux, for this current MT5 Python setup.
Python	Python 3.14.10, 64-bit	Recommended current Windows interpreter target as of this guide. Use the 64-bit installer.
Python environment	venv	Keep this project's packages isolated.
Trading terminal	MetaTrader 5 Desktop, 64-bit	Prefer the terminal installer supplied by your broker if it uses a broker-specific server/build.
Git	Current Git for Windows	Needed to clone and update the GitHub repository.
Editor	VS Code (optional)	Not required to run the bot.
AWS service	Amazon EC2 Windows instance	This is the Windows VPS hosting the terminal and bot.
AWS region	Mumbai — ap-south-1	Choose another region only after considering broker server latency and current AWS availability/cost.


Why Python 3.14.10 instead of 3.10?
The ZIP contains __pycache__ files compiled by CPython 3.10. Those are generated cache files; they do not mean the source code must run on Python 3.10. Python 3.10 reached end-of-life on 1 October 2026 and no longer receives security updates. The MetaTrader5 package currently publishes a Windows x64 wheel for CPython 3.14. Therefore, use Python 3.14.10 x64 as the installation target, then run the import and MT5 connection checks below. The bot has not been runtime-tested on this machine or on AWS as part of this documentation task.

Do not copy the ZIP's __pycache__ folder into the GitHub repository or VPS. Python will recreate cache files as needed.

Official version references:
- Python 3.14.10 release: https://www.python.org/downloads/release/python-31410/
- Python version support schedule: https://devguide.python.org/versions/
- MetaTrader5 package files: https://pypi.org/project/MetaTrader5/
