Broker symbol names must match
The supplied main.py currently lists these symbols in its four pipeline configurations:
"GOLD"
"EURUSD"
"GBPUSD"
The actual names are broker-specific. A broker may use names such as XAUUSD, XAUUSDm or another suffix rather than GOLD. Check the exact names in MT5 Market Watch and update the four symbol lists in main.py only after checking the code and broker specifications. Also inspect the scalping whitelist in execution.py before adding a symbol to scalping.
Enable Python trading only when ready
The MT5 terminal has a protective setting that can block trading operations coming from the external Python API.
1. In MT5, open Tools → Options → Expert Advisors (or press Ctrl+O).
2. Find Disable automated trading via external Python API.
3. Keep Python trading blocked while performing connection-only checks.
4. Only when you are deliberately ready to test order execution on the DEMO account, review MT5's automated-trading permissions and the account permissions, then make sure the external-Python restriction is not blocking the test.
Changing this permission can allow Python code to place orders. Do not enable it on a live account as part of installation. MetaQuotes documents this setting in its platform settings guide: https://www.metatrader5.com/en/terminal/help/startworking/settings.
