22. AWS cost and shutdown notes
Before launching, use https://calculator.aws/ and select the Mumbai (ap-south-1) region, Windows EC2, the exact instance type, expected hours per month and EBS volume. Include any public IPv4 and data-transfer costs shown by AWS and check the estimate again before changing instance sizes.
- Running: EC2 compute charges accrue while the instance is running.
- Stopped: compute billing generally stops, but EBS volumes and certain allocated network resources can continue to incur charges.
- Terminated: the instance is deleted; any EBS volumes configured to persist may continue to incur charges. Back up needed data first.
- Bot consequence: a stopped or terminated instance cannot run MT5 or the Python bot.
A 24/7 bot deployment means the Windows instance, terminal and bot process must remain operational. AWS uptime does not guarantee the broker terminal, broker connection, market data feed or trading logic will remain healthy.
